<BODY STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif">

<P STYLE="margin: 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="text-align: right; margin: 0"><B>Exhibit 99.1</B></P>

<P STYLE="margin: 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><B>APTIV ANNOUNCES CASH TENDER OFFER FOR 3.250% SENIOR NOTES DUE 2032,
5.150% SENIOR NOTES DUE 2034, 5.750% SENIOR NOTES DUE 2054, 5.400% SENIOR NOTES DUE 2049, 4.400% SENIOR NOTES DUE 2046, 4.150% SENIOR
NOTES DUE 2052 AND 3.100% SENIOR NOTES DUE 2051</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">March 6, 2026</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><B>SCHAFFHAUSEN</B>&mdash;Aptiv PLC (&ldquo;Aptiv&rdquo;) (NYSE: APTV),
a global technology company focused on enabling a more automated, electrified and digitalized future, today announced that its wholly-owned
subsidiary, Aptiv Swiss Holdings Limited, a Jersey incorporated private limited company (the &ldquo;Company&rdquo;), commenced a cash
tender offer (the &ldquo;Tender Offer&rdquo;) to purchase the outstanding notes listed in the table below (collectively, the &ldquo;Notes&rdquo;
and each a &ldquo;Series&rdquo; of Notes) for aggregate consideration of up to $1,350,000,000, exclusive of any accrued interest through
the payment date of the Notes (as it may be increased or decreased by the Company in accordance with applicable law, the &ldquo;Maximum
Aggregate Consideration&rdquo;), in the order of priority, and subject to the Series Caps shown in the table below.&nbsp;&nbsp;Capitalized
terms used in this news release and not defined herein have the meanings given to them in the Offer to Purchase.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

